# Op2_BounceY: the bounce settling (ruling 5, 2), at its first call (an object landing): half the
# landing move $3C(a3) not above the y acceleration $28(a3), so the y velocity and target speed
# are cleared instead of reversed. A real state: every bounce loses speed until it settles; the
# corpus's bouncers leave before they do.

case settle
l a3 + $28 = $00001000
l a3 + $3C = $00001000
